  "title": "Direct gravitational phase test using harmonic fit phases",
  "timestamp": "2026-09-07T12:22:44.547605+00:00",
  "design": "For each station pair, the gravitational prediction for the M2 phase difference is 2*(lon1-lon2), purely longitude-dependent. The test correlates cos(expected_dphase) with cos(observed_dphase) from harmonic fitting. Control frequencies should show no longitude dependence. S2 (solar) has both gravitational and atmospheric components, so it should also show longitude dependence but with additional scatter from atmospheric phase variations. O1 (lunar diurnal) has phase difference 1*(lon1-lon2).",
